{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(dramatic music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833,
    "dDurationMs": 997,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] A single sentence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1830,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in one of the oldest math books"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3540,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "held the key to\nunderstanding our universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6810,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Euclid's \"Elements\" has been\npublished in more editions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9690,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than any other book except the Bible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12420,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was the go to math\ntext for over 2,000 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16830,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for all that time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18030,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mathematicians were\nskeptical of a single line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21390,
    "dDurationMs": 2103,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which seemed like a mistake."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24360,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultimately, some of the\ngreatest math minds realized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27840,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Euclid wasn't wrong after all,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30630,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there was more to the story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32880,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Slight tweaks to this line\nopened up strange new universes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37170,
    "dDurationMs": 843,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out of nothing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39030,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Surprisingly, 80 years later,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41130,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we found out those strange new universes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44100,
    "dDurationMs": 3963,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are core to understanding\nour own universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51735,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(contemplative music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52568,
    "dDurationMs": 1492,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Around 300 BC,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54060,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Greek mathematician, Euclid,\ntakes on a massive project"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57570,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to summarize all mathematics\nknown at the time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60840,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to essentially create the one book"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62700,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that contains everything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64230,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that everyone knows about mathematics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67290,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's no easy task."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69330,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, before Euclid, there was\na bit of a problem with math."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73320,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- People would prove things,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75000,
    "dDurationMs": 1507,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they would just be\ngoing around in circles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76507,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Why does a triangle have 180 degrees?\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78517,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"'Cause if you take two parallel lines -\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79747,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Yeah, but why do parallel lines exist?\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81067,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Oh, that's because you can make a square."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82537,
    "dDurationMs": 1043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Why does a square exist?\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83580,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have this infinite recursion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84840,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of what the fundamental reason\nwhy something is true is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89280,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] It's kind of\nlike in the dictionary,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90810,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every word is defined\nin terms of other words,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93960,
    "dDurationMs": 2013,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so how do you get to ground truth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96900,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Euclid used a solution that\nwas pioneered by the Greeks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100680,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's just accept a few of\nthe most simple, basic things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104790,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as being true, these are our postulates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108180,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, based upon these postulates,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109980,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can prove theorems one at a time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112440,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "building up our math using logic,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114630,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that as long as those\nfirst statements are true,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117150,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then everything else\nthat follows from them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119340,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must definitely be true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122100,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He had perfected the gold standard"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124470,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for rigorous mathematical proof"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126480,
    "dDurationMs": 2313,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that all modern math relies on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130020,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Euclid used this method"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131340,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when he published his 13 book\nseries called, \"The Elements,\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134790,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in which he proved 465 theorems,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137670,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "covering almost all of\nmathematics known at the time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140700,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including geometry and number theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143970,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And all these theorems depended\non were some definitions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147600,
    "dDurationMs": 3003,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a few common notions, and five postulates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153000,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We go right to book one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154590,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and book one starts with definitions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156150,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you gotta start somewhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157290,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the definition is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158123,
    "dDurationMs": 2167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"A point is that which has no part."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160290,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A line is a breadthless length.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162360,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, \"The ends of lines are points.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165270,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By line, he really means a curve,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167310,
    "dDurationMs": 1627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then it has some ends."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168937,
    "dDurationMs": 2903,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"A straight line is a\nline that lies evenly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171840,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "within the points on itself.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173880,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then so on, and so forth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175650,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He's got 23 definitions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177540,
    "dDurationMs": 1453,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then he's got the five postulates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178993,
    "dDurationMs": 1457,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(energetic music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180450,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] The first four are simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182490,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One, if you have two points,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184350,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can draw a straight line between them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186780,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two, if you have a straight line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188490,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can extend it indefinitely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191040,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Three, given a center and a\nradius, you can draw a circle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195390,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the fourth is that all right angles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197820,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are equal to each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199710,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Alex] But postulate\nfive gets the big guns."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201780,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] Which is that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202920,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if a straight line falling\non two straight lines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205530,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "makes the interior angles on the same side"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208440,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less than two right angles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210630,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the two straight lines,\nif produced indefinitely,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213390,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meet on that side,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214830,
    "dDurationMs": 2823,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on which are the angles less\nthan the two right angles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218790,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What the hell is he talking about?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220020,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's a postulate?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220853,
    "dDurationMs": 1237,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like all of these are,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222090,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know, half of a sentence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223230,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they're all blatantly obvious."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224790,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then comes five, out of left field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226950,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's like an entire paragraph."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229110,
    "dDurationMs": 1172,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What is he doing?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230282,
    "dDurationMs": 958,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(contemplative music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231240,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] This made\nmathematicians suspicious;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233580,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it seemed like Euclid made a mistake."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236700,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Greek philosopher Proclus\nthought Postulate 5"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239280,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ought even to be struck outta\nthe postulates altogether,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242070,
    "dDurationMs": 1623,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for it is a theorem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244560,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if it's a theorem,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245850,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we should be able to prove it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247050,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the first four postulates,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248790,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that's what many people tried."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250920,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some, including Ptolemy and Proclus,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253140,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "believed they had\nsucceeded, but they hadn't."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256890,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, all they'd managed to do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258750,
    "dDurationMs": 3483,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was just restate Postulate\n5 in different words."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263190,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's one formulation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264960,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you have a line, and a\npoint that is not on that line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268560,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then there is a single unique line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271470,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which will be parallel to the first line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274620,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For this reason,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275453,
    "dDurationMs": 3337,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fifth postulate is often\ncalled the Parallel postulate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278790,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(contemplative music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279623,
    "dDurationMs": 1957,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the method of direct proof failed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281580,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other mathematicians, including\nal-Haytham and Omar Khayyam,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285540,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tried a different approach,\nproof by contradiction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289710,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The idea is simple,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291180,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you keep the first four\npostulates the same,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293520,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but assume that the\nfifth postulate is false."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295890,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you use those new\npostulates to prove theorems,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298770,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if that leads to a contradiction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300390,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for example, true equals false,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302550,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, then it means your new\nfifth postulate must be wrong."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305790,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, therefore, the only\nremaining option would be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307500,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Euclid's version of the\nfifth postulate is correct,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310710,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you would've proven\nthe fifth postulate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313650,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, what would it look like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314820,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if the fifth postulate were false?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316860,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, according to Euclid,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318030,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through a point not on a line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319830,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there could only be one line\nthat is parallel to the first."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323910,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One alternative is that\nthere are no parallel lines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326610,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that you could draw through that point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328890,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Well, people tried that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329790,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they realized that thin lines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331500,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had to be finite in length."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332790,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they're like, \"Well, that can't be.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335130,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] So this option was ruled out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336960,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it contradicted the second postulate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338700,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which states that lines can\nbe extended indefinitely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342060,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The other alternative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343560,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that you can draw more\nthan one parallel line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346140,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through a point not on the first line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348960,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So that's what they would do,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349793,
    "dDurationMs": 1657,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they would assume the\npostulate five fails,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351450,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they're like,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352490,
    "dDurationMs": 1338,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"This has gotta be wrong.\nWhere's the contradiction?\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353828,
    "dDurationMs": 1501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They couldn't find the contradiction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355329,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(intense acoustic music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356162,
    "dDurationMs": 2218,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] So proof by\ncontradiction also failed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358380,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In total, mathematicians\nspent more than 2,000 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361500,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trying to prove the fifth postulate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363390,
    "dDurationMs": 2193,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but everyone who tried failed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367585,
    "dDurationMs": 1895,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(contemplative music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369480,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, around 1820, János\nBolyai, a 17 year old student,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373950,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "started spending his days and\nnights working on the mystery."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377670,
    "dDurationMs": 3487,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His father became worried,\nand he wrote to his son,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381157,
    "dDurationMs": 2993,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"You must not attempt this\napproach to parallels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384150,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know this way to the very end,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386250,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have traversed this bottomless night,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388410,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which extinguished all\nlight and joy in my life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391920,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I intrigue you, leave the\nscience of parallels alone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396390,
    "dDurationMs": 1947,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Learn from my example.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399900,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the young Bolyai didn't\nlisten to his father,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402750,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he could not leave the\nscience of parallels alone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406500,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After years of work,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407790,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he realized that maybe the fifth postulate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410100,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can't be proven from the other four,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412470,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it could be completely independent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416407,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417240,
    "dDurationMs": 930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, according to Euclid,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418170,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could have only one\nparallel line through a point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421110,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Bolyai imagined a world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422490,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where there could be more\nthan one parallel line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424770,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through that point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426450,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427560,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, who said you needed\nto have a flat surface?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430770,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On a surface that is curved like this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432750,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can draw more than one line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434520,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is parallel to the original line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437250,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But wait a second, those\nlines don't look straight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440670,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, what makes straight lines special"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442560,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that they're the shortest\npaths between two points."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445470,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On this surface, those\nshortest paths just look bent,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448650,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the surface is curved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451200,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's a more familiar example."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453150,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Airplanes always try to\nfly the shortest path"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455460,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between two cities,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456570,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they're basically flying\nin a straight line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458670,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that line doesn't\nlook straight on a map"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461190,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the surface is curved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463770,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These shortest paths on curved surfaces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466110,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are called geodesics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468660,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, all these lines are straight,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470940,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they just don't look it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471990,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the world Bolyai had imagined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473700,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turned out to be curved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475440,
    "dDurationMs": 2733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We now know this as hyperbolic geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480630,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You know, when I used to\nthink of the hyperbolic plane,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483150,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would just imagine\nit as one giant saddle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486270,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's not really what it is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488370,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the hyperbolic plane is much more like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490170,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this piece of crocheting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492450,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, it starts out pretty\nflat and even in the middle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495420,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as you move outwards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497310,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more and more fabric is created,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500310,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that would push parallel lines apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504420,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the further and further out you go,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506310,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the amount of fabric grows exponentially,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508890,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that ends up causing\nthis crumpling effect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512460,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you really wanna think\nabout the hyperbolic plane,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514860,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think you've gotta think about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516810,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "saddles, on saddles, on saddles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518370,
    "dDurationMs": 3241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like it's a infinite crumpling mess."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521611,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522444,
    "dDurationMs": 1026,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] But that little piece of crochet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523470,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn't the full hyperbolic plane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525600,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To show that, we need to make a map,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527970,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one that fits the entire\nplane into a disc."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 532020,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To show how this works,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533100,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're gonna fill the entire\nplane with these triangles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536190,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Starting in the middle,\njust as with the crochet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538410,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "things look pretty normal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540120,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as you go farther out from the center,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542520,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get all this extra space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544170,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you can fit more and more triangles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546990,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they appear smaller,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548730,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they are actually the same size."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551880,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, since the hyperbolic\nplane is infinite,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554040,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can keep adding triangles forever,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556320,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they all need to fit on the disk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558840,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So as you get closer to the edge,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560460,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the triangles will appear\nsmaller, and smaller, and smaller,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564330,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "infinitely smaller, never ending,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566460,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you can never quite reach the edge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569790,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is known as the Poincare Disk Model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572580,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, straight lines are arcs of circles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574890,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that intersect the disc at 90 degrees,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577650,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and just like on our original shape,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579480,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a straight line down the\nmiddle appears straight,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582210,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while straight lines next\nto it appear to curve away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586200,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's remarkable is that\nBolyai didn't have a model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589260,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of hyperbolic geometry yet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591180,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he was just drawing Euclidean\ntriangles with the assumption"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594330,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Euclid's fifth postulate didn't hold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596940,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And while Bolyai found"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598710,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the behavior in hyperbolic geometry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600570,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is very different than Euclid's,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602730,
    "dDurationMs": 3384,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mathematically, it seemed\njust as consistent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606114,
    "dDurationMs": 1656,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607770,
    "dDurationMs": 4207,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1823, the 20-year-old\nJános wrote to his dad,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611977,
    "dDurationMs": 4313,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"I have discovered such wonderful\nthings that I was amazed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616290,
    "dDurationMs": 4617,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Out of nothing, I have created\na strange new universe.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623991,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(contemplative music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624824,
    "dDurationMs": 856,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Bolyai had been doing more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625680,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than just tackling ancient math mysteries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 628320,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In his twenties, he joined the army,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630300,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where he continued developing\ntwo of his other passions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632970,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "playing the violin and dueling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636180,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He had mastered both,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637830,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but with a sword in\nparticular, he was unmatched."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641250,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps because of his many\ntalents, Bolyai grew arrogant,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644160,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and found it difficult to accept authority"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645810,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from his superiors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647250,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That made him hard to get along with."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650190,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This reached a peak when,\nduring one of his deployments,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653070,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "13 cavalry officers from his garrison"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655500,
    "dDurationMs": 1953,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "challenged him to a duel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658470,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bolyai accepted their challenge,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660090,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the condition that\nafter every two duels,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662430,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he could play for a little\nwhile on his violin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665820,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bolyai fought each of them in succession,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668220,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "winning all 13 duels,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670410,
    "dDurationMs": 3453,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and leaving behind all his\nadversaries on the square."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675360,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While Bolyai loved dueling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677160,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his first love was still mathematics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679620,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1832,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681030,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "9 years after he discovered\nhis strange new universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he published his findings\nas a 24 page appendix"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687360,
    "dDurationMs": 1323,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to his father's textbook."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689850,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Extremely proud and excited\nabout his son's work,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692730,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Farkas Bolyai sent it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693990,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to perhaps the greatest\nmathematician of all time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696630,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Carl Friedrich Gauss."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699150,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After careful examination,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700710,
    "dDurationMs": 1837,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gauss replied a few months later,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702547,
    "dDurationMs": 3443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"To praise it would\namount to praising myself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 705990,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the entire content of the work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708750,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coincides almost exactly\nwith my own meditations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712080,
    "dDurationMs": 3845,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which have occupied my mind\nfor the past 30 or 35 years.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715925,
    "dDurationMs": 865,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716790,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Years earlier, Gauss had\nwandered a similar path."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720090,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1824, he wrote a private\nletter to one of his friends,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723300,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in which he describes\ndiscovering a curious geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726990,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one with paradoxical,\nand to the uninitiated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730080,
    "dDurationMs": 1683,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "absurd theorems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732840,
    "dDurationMs": 1567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, Gauss writes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734407,
    "dDurationMs": 1883,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"The three angles of a triangle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736290,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "become as small as one wishes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738720,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if only the sides are taken large enough."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741750,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet the area of the triangle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743460,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can never exceed a definite limit.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746640,
    "dDurationMs": 930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747570,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can have a triangle\nthat's infinitely long,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 750540,
    "dDurationMs": 1923,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the area is finite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753570,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see why by using\nthe Poincare disk model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756600,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A small triangle looks pretty ordinary,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759030,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as you make it bigger,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760740,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the angles start to become\nsmaller and smaller."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764250,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Eventually, all those angles go to zero,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766950,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because all these lines\nintersect the disk at 90 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771090,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, these lines are infinitely long,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 773550,
    "dDurationMs": 3663,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but because of the geometry,\nthe area is finite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779040,
    "dDurationMs": 2197,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the same private letter, Gauss wrote,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781237,
    "dDurationMs": 2453,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"All my efforts to\ndiscover a contradiction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783690,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and inconsistency in this\nnon-Euclidean geometry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787440,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have been without success.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790200,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just like Bolyai, Gauss had\nfound that this geometry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792960,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "seemed thoroughly consistent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795150,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He named it non-Euclidean geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 797490,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a name that stuck."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798960,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It describes geometries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800160,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where Euclid's first four postulates hold,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802410,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the fifth doesn't."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804270,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Gauss decided not\nto publish his findings"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806430,
    "dDurationMs": 1593,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for fear of ridicule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809130,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This aversion to a\ndifferent kind of geometry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811800,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should at least be a little surprising,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813900,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because there is one other geometry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815910,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we should be very familiar\nwith, spherical geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819330,
    "dDurationMs": 2627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since we all live on a sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821957,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822790,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On a sphere, straight lines\nare parts of great circles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826050,
    "dDurationMs": 990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these are the circles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827040,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the largest possible circumference."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829440,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On Earth, the equator,\nand circles of longitude,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832110,
    "dDurationMs": 2013,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are examples of great circles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835140,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we can use this to see\nhow straight lines behave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838470,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These lines seem to go\nin the same direction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841170,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as you keep extending them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842760,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you find that they intersect once,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845580,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then again on the\nother side of the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848550,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this will always happen\nfor any two great circles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852030,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they must each"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853530,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have the largest possible circumference,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855750,
    "dDurationMs": 3903,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so, on a sphere, there\nare no parallel lines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860850,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gauss had long been fascinated\nby spherical geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 864240,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was also a geodesist,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865800,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and frequently took\nmeasurements of the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867860,
    "dDurationMs": 1270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 1820s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869130,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he was tasked with surveying\nthe Kingdom of Hanover"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871980,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to help make a map."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873690,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As part of this survey,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 874650,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he climbed the mountains near Gottingen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876960,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the help of people\nsituated on other landmarks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879330,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they were able to carefully\nmeasure the angles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881430,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of several triangles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883110,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which would then be used\nto determine the position"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885240,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of one place relative to another."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887490,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a reference for the survey,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888930,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to help determine the\nroundness of the Earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891570,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they also precisely measured\nthe angles of a large triangle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894930,
    "dDurationMs": 1773,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "formed by three mountains."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898440,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for all of Gauss' romantic notions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900780,
    "dDurationMs": 2102,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of taking measurements\non top of mountains,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902882,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(contemplative music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903715,
    "dDurationMs": 2495,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he was not the kindest correspondent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906210,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When Bolyai received his hero's response,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908700,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he was devastated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910230,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "believing that Gauss was\ntrying to undermine him"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912300,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and steal his ideas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914190,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was so embittered by Gauss' response"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916710,
    "dDurationMs": 2373,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that he never published again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920100,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1848, Bolyai had to\nendure another hardship"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 923460,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when he found out that\nRussian mathematician,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925410,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nikolai Lobachevsky,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926790,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had independently discovered\nnon-Euclidean geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929850,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "several years before Bolyai had published"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932310,
    "dDurationMs": 2403,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his 24 page long appendix."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936030,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When Bolyai died in 1860,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 938250,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he left behind 20,000 pages"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940740,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of unpublished mathematical manuscripts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 943380,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He would not know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944430,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Gauss did independently discover"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946650,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "non-Euclidean geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 948330,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nor would he know, that\nupon receiving the appendix,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950640,
    "dDurationMs": 2227,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gauss had written to a friend,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952867,
    "dDurationMs": 2573,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"I regard this young geometer, Bolyai,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955440,
    "dDurationMs": 3492,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a genius of the first order.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958932,
    "dDurationMs": 2358,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 961290,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While Bolyai was embittered,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963030,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "non-Euclidean geometries\ncontinued to develop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966360,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Until 1854, spherical geometry\nwasn't actually considered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970650,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a non-Euclidean geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973050,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because, on a sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974760,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lines can't be extended indefinitely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977610,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what earlier\nmathematicians had stumbled upon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979950,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and therefore dismissed this geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 981990,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since Euclid's second\npostulate wouldn't hold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 985530,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in 1854,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987120,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Riemann changed the second postulate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989160,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from an infinite extension"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 991050,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to something that is, quote, \"unbounded,\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993690,
    "dDurationMs": 3243,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that the second postulate\nstill holds on a sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998160,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With this change,\nspherical geometry became"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000680,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "another valid non-Euclidean geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1003590,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By using the generalized four postulates,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005930,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and taking the fifth as there\nbeing no parallel lines,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008960,
    "dDurationMs": 3663,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could now derive spherical\nor elliptic geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1013850,
    "dDurationMs": 3123,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Would you consider the\nfifth postulate a mistake?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1017870,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Would it have been better if\nhe just never wrote that down?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020570,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If he never wrote that down,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1021740,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he would've stunted his geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023060,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "'cause he wouldn't be able to prove"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024320,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lot of things that he claimed to have."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026600,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's beautiful that he wrote this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1029270,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's beautiful that\npeople spent 2,000 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1031580,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trying to refute him,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032810,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only to discover that,\nin fact, he was right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035900,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in writing this in the first place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038270,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] So, while Euclid was right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040040,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to write down the fifth postulate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041720,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he did make a different mistake."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1044600,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So here's the problem\nwith what Euclid was doing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1046670,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Definition 1, \"A point is\nthat which has no part.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1050540,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What does it mean to have a part?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1051740,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What is a part?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053090,
    "dDurationMs": 1177,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What does it mean not to have a part?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1054267,
    "dDurationMs": 3083,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"A line is a breadthless length.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1057350,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What does it mean to have breadth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058640,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lying evenly within itself,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060230,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "within the points on itself?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061700,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What the hell is he talking about?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1063110,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We read this two minutes ago,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064820,
    "dDurationMs": 937,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we were nodding along like,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1065757,
    "dDurationMs": 2363,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Yeah, completely makes\nsense what he's saying.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1068120,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's all nonsense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069350,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Don't give me a definition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071150,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's gonna have an infinite recursion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073340,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you give me a definition\nin terms of other things,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075320,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you have to tell me\nwhat those things are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1076880,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you tell me what that is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077713,
    "dDurationMs": 2107,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you have to tell me what\nthe thing before it is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1079820,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Are the definitions a bad idea?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1082970,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You shouldn't have definitions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1085160,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you should have undefined terms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1087170,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm not gonna tell you what a point is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088580,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm not gonna tell you what a line is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1089720,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm not gonna tell you what a plane is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1091430,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All I'm gonna tell you is\nwhat the postulates are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094880,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they're assumed to satisfy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1096530,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the relationships between\nthe objects that's important,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099530,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not the definitions of\nthe objects themselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1101990,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And once you free your\nmind to that possibility,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105050,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of a sudden,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106070,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you realize that there's a\nperfectly good geometric world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109160,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in which, by line, you mean great circle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1111710,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by plane, you mean sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1113600,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by point, you mean\na point on a sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116540,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then four of those\naxioms are satisfied,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119210,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just not the fifth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1120560,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And similarly, there's another model,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1122930,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something called a disk\nmodel for hyperbolic space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1125570,
    "dDurationMs": 1713,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which, the disk is the plane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128570,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What I mean by straight lines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1129950,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is arcs of circles that\nare orthogonal to the disk,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1132890,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then points are\npoints inside the disk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1135620,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the disk is the plane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138200,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] See, you can\nthink of geometry as a game."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140400,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(thoughtful music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1141233,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first four postulates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142066,
    "dDurationMs": 3184,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are like the minimum rules\nrequired to play that game,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1145250,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then the fifth postulate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1146810,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "selects the world that you'll play in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1149720,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you pick that there\nare no parallel lines,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1151610,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're playing in spherical geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1153740,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you choose one parallel line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155660,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're playing in flat geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1157490,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you go for more\nthan one parallel line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159890,
    "dDurationMs": 2463,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you're playing in\nhyperbolic geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1163730,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Riemann decided to\ntake it one step further."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1166640,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of selecting just\none world to play in,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1169430,
    "dDurationMs": 2463,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why not combine them all into one?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1173330,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "During his inaugural speech in 1854,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1175910,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he laid out the groundwork for a geometry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1178010,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the curvature could\ndiffer from place to place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1181040,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One part might be flat,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1182510,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "another part might be slightly curved,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1184490,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and yet another part might\nhave a very strong curvature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1187820,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this geometry wouldn't be limited"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1189710,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to two-dimensional planes either,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1191780,
    "dDurationMs": 3393,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it could be extended to\nthree or more dimensions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196623,
    "dDurationMs": 947,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(contemplative music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1197570,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Another breakthrough came in 1868,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1200000,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when Eugenio Beltrami unequivocally proved"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1202640,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that hyperbolic and spherical geometry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204830,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were just as consistent\nas Euclid's flat geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208160,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, if there were any inconsistencies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1210380,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in hyperbolic or spherical geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1212630,
    "dDurationMs": 3693,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then they must also be present\nin Euclid's flat geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1217190,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The prospects for these new\ngeometries were looking great."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1220400,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it turns out, this\nwas just the beginning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1223850,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1224683,
    "dDurationMs": 3697,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1905, Einstein proposed the\nspecial theory of relativity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1228380,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is based on just two postulates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1230780,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One, \"The laws of physics are the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1232550,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in all inertial frames of reference.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1234830,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And two, \"The speed of light in a vacuum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1237380,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the same for all inertial observers.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1240440,
    "dDurationMs": 4563,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, as a result, space\nand time must be relative."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1246200,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that created a problem\nfor Newtonian gravity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1249140,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because, according to Newton,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1250790,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the force of gravity is\ninversely proportional"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253280,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the distance between\nthe two objects squared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1256070,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in Einstein's special relativity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1258080,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that distance is no longer well-defined."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1261140,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In whose reference frame are we measuring?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1263840,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so Einstein had to\nfind a way to reconcile"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1267020,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relativity and gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1269420,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two years later, in 1907,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1271310,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Einstein had the happiest\nthought of his life,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274340,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he imagined a man falling\noff the roof of a house."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1277280,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what made Einstein so joyful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1279050,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that he realized that\nwhile the man is falling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1281480,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he would feel absolutely weightless,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1283820,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if he let go of an object,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285320,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it would just remain in\nuniform motion relative to him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1289010,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would be just like being\nin space, not near any masses,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1293210,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "floating around in a spaceship\nat constant velocity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1296210,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that is an inertial observer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299210,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, here's the big breakthrough,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1301040,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Einstein realized that\nthey're not just similar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1303590,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are identical,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1305120,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because there is no\nexperiment you could do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1307250,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to determine whether you're in free fall"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1309200,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a uniform gravitational field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1311180,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or whether you are in deep space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1312950,
    "dDurationMs": 2133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not near any massive objects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316160,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so the free-falling man too"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1318410,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must be an inertial observer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1320330,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning he is not accelerating,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1322340,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he's not experiencing\nany force of gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1325970,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if gravity is not a force,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328040,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then how do you explain things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1329300,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the space station orbiting Earth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1331550,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Shouldn't it just fly\noff in a straight line?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1334550,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, astronauts in the space\nstation also feel weightless."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1338000,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's the key,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1339350,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it feels just as if they're\ntraveling at constant velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1342380,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a straight line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1343910,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It feels like that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1345020,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because that's precisely\nwhat they're doing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1347570,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they're traveling in a straight line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1350030,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How, then, could that\nstraight line appear curved"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1352280,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a distant observer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1354170,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1355003,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the space time that\nstraight line is on is curved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1360650,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, massive objects curve spacetime,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1363440,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and objects moving\nthrough curved spacetime"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1365510,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will follow the shortest path\nthrough that curved geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1368780,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the geodesic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1370070,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, while astronauts in the space station"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1371810,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are following a straight line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1373460,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it appears curved to a distant observer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1375710,
    "dDurationMs": 3243,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the Earth curves\nthe spacetime around it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380690,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, the behavior of straight\nlines in curved geometries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1383900,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is core to understanding\nthe universe we live in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1387170,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in the more than a hundred\nyears since it was published,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1389810,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the general theory of relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1391400,
    "dDurationMs": 3081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been remarkably successful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1394481,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1395314,
    "dDurationMs": 3376,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2014, astronomers briefly\nobserved a supernova,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1398690,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a violent and extremely\nbright death of a star."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1402170,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, they saw the exact same supernova"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1404300,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in four different places."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1406520,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1407480,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, in between the supernova and earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1409610,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there was a massive galaxy,\nwhich curved space time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1413060,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so light from the supernova,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1414440,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which was spreading out in all directions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1416510,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had several different\npaths to reach the earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1419330,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and four of those reached Earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1420830,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at approximately the same time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1422780,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The galaxy had functioned as\na massive gravitational lens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1427220,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The astronomers realized that\nother galaxies in the cluster"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1430250,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "might also lens the light\nfrom that supernova,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1433160,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but with different path lengths"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1434750,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and gravitational potentials,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1436400,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the light would reach\nearth at different times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1440000,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After careful modeling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1441500,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they predicted that\nthey should see a replay"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1443960,
    "dDurationMs": 2613,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of that supernova just a year later."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1447650,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And on the 11th of December, 2015,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1450020,
    "dDurationMs": 4143,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just as predicted, they saw\nthe same supernova once more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1455870,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In addition to being able\nto observe the effects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1457940,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of curved spacetime,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1459290,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can now even measure the\nripples of space time itself,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1462590,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gravitational waves\nformed by cosmic events,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1465230,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "far, far away,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1467000,
    "dDurationMs": 1983,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the merger of black holes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1469880,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And according to a recent\nsurvey by NANOGrav,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1472910,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fabric of spacetime\nseems to be buzzing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1475400,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the remnants of grand cosmic events."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1478880,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the hundred years since\ngeneral relativity was published,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1481760,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "countless findings have\nsupported its predictions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1484310,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and at its very core are\nthe curved geometries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1487610,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Bolyai and Riemann."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1489980,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But so far, all the\neffects we've looked at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1492080,
    "dDurationMs": 2673,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are local distortions of spacetime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1495590,
    "dDurationMs": 2713,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What is the shape of the entire universe?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1498303,
    "dDurationMs": 1752,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(stars whooshing)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500055,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(contemplative music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500888,
    "dDurationMs": 1902,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Using the differences\nbetween the geometries,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1502790,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can find that out too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1504920,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In flat geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1506090,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we expect all the angles of a triangle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1508160,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to add up to 180 degrees without fail."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1511160,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in spherical geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1512720,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the angles don't add up to\n180 degrees, but to more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1516530,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly in hyperbolic geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1518390,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the angles add up to\nless than 180 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1521660,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, to determine the\nshape of the universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1524180,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you just need to measure\nthe angles of a triangle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1527480,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And measuring a triangle is\nprecisely what Gauss was doing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1530360,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "200 years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1531830,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, this led some to speculate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1533990,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that he was actually trying\nto measure the curvature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1535970,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of space itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1537950,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The angle he found,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1539780,
    "dDurationMs": 2793,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "180 degrees, within observational error."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1543770,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that shouldn't be very surprising."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546170,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Take this balloon, for example,\nwhich approximates a sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1549830,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If I draw a small triangle on it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1552500,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, the surface I'm\ndrawing on is basically flat,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1555290,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the angles inside the triangle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1556790,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will add up to essentially 180 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1559700,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Only if I make the triangle large enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1562850,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will the effects of\ncurvature come into play,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1565970,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then the angles in the triangle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1567620,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will add up to more than 180 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1570110,
    "dDurationMs": 2064,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this was the problem\nwith Gauss' experiment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1572174,
    "dDurationMs": 2676,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even if he was trying\nto measure the curvature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1574850,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of space itself, for which\nthere is no solid evidence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1578240,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the triangle he measured\nwould've been far too small"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1581240,
    "dDurationMs": 3232,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relative to the size of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1584472,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(ball thudding)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1585305,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1586138,
    "dDurationMs": 2032,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, in order to overcome the scale issue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1588170,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Gauss encountered,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1589460,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we need to scale the triangles\nformed between mountains"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1592220,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up to the largest triangles we can."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1594860,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since looking further and further away"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1597050,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the same as looking\nfurther back in time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1599540,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we need to look back as far as possible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1602390,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the very first light we can see,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1605210,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Cosmic Microwave Background, or CMB,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1608420,
    "dDurationMs": 4503,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a picture from when the universe\nwas just 380,000 years old."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1613790,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While the CMB is almost\ncompletely uniform,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1616640,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are some spots that are\nslightly hotter or colder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1620300,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, we know how far away the CMB is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1622910,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if we can figure out\nhow large such a spot is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1626060,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then we can draw a cosmic triangle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1629570,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's thought that the first density"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1631280,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and temperature variations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1632510,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "originated from quantum fluctuations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1634910,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the very early universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1636560,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which were then blown up\nas the universe expanded."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1639590,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But due to this rapid expansion,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1641570,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not all regions were in causal\ncontact with each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1645590,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, using the information we have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1647570,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of how the early universe evolved,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1649520,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "astronomers can predict how\noften spots of different sizes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1653150,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should appear in the CMB."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1655790,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what this power spectrum shows,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1658520,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "essentially a histogram of how often"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1660920,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each spot size should occur\nif the universe is flat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1665000,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now we have something to\ncompare our measurement to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1668390,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the universe is flat,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1669740,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the angle we measure on the sky"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1671120,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should be the same as we'd expect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1673550,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if the universe is\ncurved like a sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1675770,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the angles of the triangle should add up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1677600,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to more than 180 degrees,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1680000,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the angle we'd measure\nwould be larger than predicted,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1683300,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this peak would shift to the left."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1685880,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, if the universe\nhas hyperbolic geometry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1689030,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then spots should appear\nsmaller than predicted,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1691700,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this peak would shift to the right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1694520,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, what do we measure?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1696500,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the data from the Plank mission,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1698240,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is almost exactly what you'd expect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1700610,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if the universe were flat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1702530,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This mission also gives us\nthe current best estimate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1704960,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the curvature of the universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1706490,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is 0.0007, plus minus 0.0019."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1711830,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that's basically zero\nwithin the margin of error."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1715730,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we're fairly certain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1717020,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the universe we live in is flat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1722120,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But living in a flat universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1723590,
    "dDurationMs": 1941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "seems to be remarkably serendipitous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1725531,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(contemplative music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1726364,
    "dDurationMs": 1816,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right now, the average mass energy density"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1728180,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "comes down to the equivalent\nof about six hydrogen atoms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1730940,
    "dDurationMs": 1023,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "per cubic meter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1732890,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If, on average, that was\njust one more hydrogen atom,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1735860,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the universe would've been\nmore spherically curved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1738680,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If there were just one less,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1740330,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the curvature would be\nhyperbolic geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1743090,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so far, we're not\nentirely sure why the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1745790,
    "dDurationMs": 2073,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has the mass energy density it has."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1749120,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What we do know is that general relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1751370,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is one of our best physical\ntheories of reality,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1754070,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and at the very heart of it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1755750,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are those paradoxical and\nseemingly absurd geometries,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1759830,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ones we found because mathematicians\nspent over 2,000 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1763790,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thinking about a single sentence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1765830,
    "dDurationMs": 3143,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the world's most famous math text."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1768973,
    "dDurationMs": 3083,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(high-tech blooping)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1773390,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When it comes to human brilliance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1775130,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's not just what you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1776930,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's also how you think,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1778700,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a great way to improve how you think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1781130,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is by building your knowledge\nand problem solving skills."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1784190,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you're looking\nfor a free and easy way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1786770,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to do just that,"
    } ]
